  "body": "Hi, \r\n\r\nI'm trying to use a filter to get only messages in my room timeline, my filter looks like this:\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n    \"room\": {\r\n        \"timeline\": {\r\n            \"limit\": 1,\r\n            \"types\": [\r\n                \"m.room.message\",\r\n                \"m.room.encrypted\",\r\n            ]\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n```\r\nThe problem is that when I'm using this filter I only get old state events even though I haven't specified a filter on them, for example when I update the ```m.room.power_levels```, the change takes effect but I don't get the updated state when I'm using that filter so I tried explicitly specifying the state filter and got the same result, then I thought it might be the limit and tried that too but it was the same.\r\n\r\nMy filter ended up looking like this:\r\n```\r\n{\r\n    \"room\": {\r\n        \"state\": {\r\n            \"limit\": 9007199254740991, (Yes, I know it's absurd)\r\n            \"types\": [\r\n                \"*\",\r\n                \"m.room.create\",\r\n                \"m.room.power_levels\",\r\n                \"m.room.name\",\r\n                \"m.room.member\",\r\n            ]\r\n        },\r\n        \"timeline\": {\r\n            \"limit\": 1,\r\n            \"types\": [\r\n                \"m.room.message\",\r\n                \"m.room.encrypted\"\r\n            ]\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nI'm using a Synapse Homeserver, Installed using pip version 1.25.0\r\n\r\n\r\n",
